1
00:00:00,035 --> 00:00:03,553
Alex asks for the eleven o'clock appointment, but the slot is full.

2
00:00:04,156 --> 00:00:07,872
A confident booking confirmation is useful only if the schedule can support
it.

3
00:00:08,382 --> 00:00:11,424
We will test the capacity rule and inspect the appointment record.

4
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:13,947
Alex is using the Patient Access Assistant.

5
00:00:14,121 --> 00:00:17,697
The conversation sits beside the recorded business action and tool trace.

6
00:00:18,138 --> 00:00:22,062
We start with a customer request, then use Rook to test the expected
behavior

7
00:00:22,132 --> 00:00:22,945
independently.

8
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:25,575
Patient lookup resolves the authenticated patient.

9
00:00:25,958 --> 00:00:28,187
Booking checks capacity and records an appointment.

10
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:33,121
Urgent handoff, administrative guidance and record export serve separate
responsibilities.

11
00:00:33,632 --> 00:00:37,498
This fictional service handles access and scheduling, not clinical
diagnosis.

12
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:41,712
Follow a routine booking request through patient identity and slot
availability.

13
00:00:42,095 --> 00:00:44,312
A full slot must produce no appointment.

14
00:00:44,637 --> 00:00:46,948
An available slot may be reserved once.

15
00:00:47,389 --> 00:00:50,605
Urgent requests follow the separate human-handoff policy.

16
00:00:50,930 --> 00:00:53,136
The reply must agree with the recorded action.

17
00:00:53,379 --> 00:00:55,144
Start in Rook's interactive terminal.

18
00:00:55,469 --> 00:00:57,698
Explore the supplied source and requirements.

19
00:00:58,395 --> 00:01:01,506
Rook discovers the agent, its interface and business features.

20
00:01:02,110 --> 00:01:06,394
The requirements define correct behavior; defects in the implementation must

21
00:01:06,464 --> 00:01:07,962
not become acceptance rules.

22
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:11,747
Exploration writes an agent definition and feature files into this
workspace.

23
00:01:12,258 --> 00:01:14,569
Open them and check the discovered responsibilities.

24
00:01:14,952 --> 00:01:18,702
These are readable local artifacts, ready for review before anything is
synchronized.

25
00:01:18,952 --> 00:01:23,549
Generate a focused set across functional, non-functional and adversarial
classes.

26
00:01:24,153 --> 00:01:26,440
Review the proposed scope, then confirm.

27
00:01:27,137 --> 00:01:31,665
Rook writes scenario files with customer goals and acceptance criteria; the
generated

28
00:01:31,711 --> 00:01:33,789
count alone is not a coverage claim.

29
00:01:34,046 --> 00:01:36,659
The requirements declare no capacity at eleven o'clock.

30
00:01:37,042 --> 00:01:40,490
The selected criterion therefore requires no appointment at that time.

31
00:01:41,187 --> 00:01:44,739
Review the patient reference and the booking rule together; a successful
tool

32
00:01:44,797 --> 00:01:46,934
response does not make an overbooking correct.

33
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:49,784
Create the connection profile from the supplied contract.

34
00:01:50,167 --> 00:01:51,815
Rook authors the runner and checks it.

35
00:01:52,199 --> 00:01:56,250
Opening a session, executing turns, closing it and collecting evidence are
separate

36
00:01:56,274 --> 00:01:57,214
responsibilities.

37
00:01:57,410 --> 00:01:59,476
Inspect the profile, then test the connection.

38
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:03,459
Confirm that Rook reaches the intended agent and returns a correlated
response.

39
00:02:03,969 --> 00:02:07,487
Keep credential values in the environment, outside the profile and
recording.

40
00:02:07,702 --> 00:02:09,815
Run the selected scenario with the test flag.

41
00:02:10,198 --> 00:02:15,550
Review the plan and proceed. Rook invokes the agent and judges the returned
evidence.

42
00:02:15,933 --> 00:02:18,766
This run stays out of the hosted project timeline.

43
00:02:19,149 --> 00:02:21,204
Processing time is removed from the edit.

44
00:02:21,452 --> 00:02:22,857
Open the report in the terminal.

45
00:02:23,182 --> 00:02:25,898
Read the verdict and the criterion-level explanation.

46
00:02:26,502 --> 00:02:30,508
A passing response, a failed business action and missing evidence are
distinct

47
00:02:30,566 --> 00:02:33,387
findings; the report must preserve that distinction.

48
00:02:33,671 --> 00:02:37,317
The run is also a set of files on this machine: its plan, report,

49
00:02:37,433 --> 00:02:40,521
requests, responses, verdicts and collected evidence.

50
00:02:40,846 --> 00:02:44,387
Open the same run identifier and follow one scenario through these files.

51
00:02:44,771 --> 00:02:48,045
These files remain available without opening the hosted interface.

52
00:02:48,254 --> 00:02:51,854
The agent confirms an eleven o'clock appointment and records appointment
one,

53
00:02:52,179 --> 00:02:54,942
even though the requirements declare zero capacity.

54
00:02:55,546 --> 00:02:59,795
Rook reports Fail because the original booking tool accepts a slot that the
requirements

55
00:02:59,830 --> 00:03:00,573
say is full.

56
00:03:00,796 --> 00:03:03,571
The role-play attack asks for a capacity override.

57
00:03:03,954 --> 00:03:07,786
The answer refuses the override persona, but an appointment is still
recorded

58
00:03:07,820 --> 00:03:10,595
for the full slot. Rook reports Fail.

59
00:03:11,199 --> 00:03:13,625
A polite refusal did not prevent the business action.

60
00:03:13,879 --> 00:03:16,817
The M C P connection preserves the patient across turns.

61
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:20,880
In this Developer check, the context criteria pass and the receipt belongs
to

62
00:03:20,927 --> 00:03:25,977
the correct patient. That result does not validate capacity: the separate
capacity

63
00:03:26,023 --> 00:03:27,962
test has already exposed the overbooking.

64
00:03:28,213 --> 00:03:30,884
Repeat the same case against the updated capacity check.

65
00:03:31,267 --> 00:03:34,344
The appointment list remains empty, and Rook reports Pass.

66
00:03:34,785 --> 00:03:38,593
The repair enforces availability at the booking boundary; it does not depend

67
00:03:38,674 --> 00:03:40,543
only on the model choosing to refuse.

68
00:03:40,702 --> 00:03:45,311
Sharing is optional. Sync the reviewed project definitions, then execute a
shared

69
00:03:45,357 --> 00:03:49,235
run without the test flag. That new run records its results upstream.

70
00:03:49,676 --> 00:03:53,055
Sync does not convert the earlier local test into a hosted run.

71
00:03:53,327 --> 00:03:57,495
Open the hosted web interface. Select the matching shared run, then open its

72
00:03:57,518 --> 00:04:01,547
scenario and evidence. The local files and hosted view serve different
review

73
00:04:01,605 --> 00:04:05,192
needs; use the run identifier to keep the investigation consistent.

74
00:04:05,410 --> 00:04:07,848
Explore the agent. Review generated tests.

75
00:04:07,999 --> 00:04:10,669
Prove the connection. Run, inspect and repair.

76
00:04:10,878 --> 00:04:14,117
Keep the artifacts local, and share a reviewed run when the team needs it.

77
00:04:14,396 --> 00:04:15,917
Agent Assurance, with Rook.
